{"name":"Pandora Grey","hex":"#e3d4cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pandora","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any fish of the genus Pagellus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pandora"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pandora","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Pandora was the first human woman, created by Hephaestus on the instructions of Zeus. As Hesiod related it, each deity cooperated by giving her unique gifts. Her other name—inscribed against her figure on a white-ground kylix in the British Museum—is Anesidora."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Abel-josef-1764-1818-austria-prometheus-merkur-und-die-pand.jpg/330px-Abel-josef-1764-1818-austria-prometheus-merkur-und-die-pand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandora","wikidata":"Q131346"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Pandora_-_John_William_Waterhouse.jpg/500px-Pandora_-_John_William_Waterhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wi